Title:  A Meaningful Life

Seq:    12.6.72.1.2

Level:  6 - Subdetail

Class:  quote

Attribution: [[Harari, Yuval Noah|Yuval Noah Harari]], 2015, from the book *[[Sapiens: A Brief History of Humankind]]*

Timestamp: 20251022235715

Date Added: 2025-10-22 17:57:15 -0600

Date Modified: 2026-10-15 12:27:06 -0600

Referenced In: We seek meaning

Body:

As Nietzsche put it, if you have a why to live, you can bear almost any how. A meaningful life can be extremely satisfying even in the midst of hardship, whereas a meaningless life is a terrible ordeal no matter how comfortable it is.

